# NF-W2b flip-tracking local copies: the retained SERVED-board snapshot's canonical home is
# s3://credence-prod-s3-api-cache/snapshots/<tag>/ (immutable); --download copies are a local
# convenience, never committed (a convenience commit must not sweep prod JSON into git).
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/artifacts/served_board_snapshots/
# NF-INJ2b — the PUBLISHED 2026 board, staged from the prod api-cache as the study's baseline.
# 1.3 MB and re-fetchable in one command; the runner REFUSES with that command named rather than
# dying opaquely or (worse) substituting a rebuild for it (NF-INFRA1's cure: a gitignored artifact a
# build READS must fail with a named remedy). The small `manifest.json` beside it IS committed —
# it is the vintage/provenance record the report cites.
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/artifacts/nf_inj2b_baseline/served_projections_*.json
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/artifacts/nf_inj2b_baseline/board_2026_*.parquet
# NF-INJ2c (PM ruling, decision request #5): the D3 CAPTURE STAMP is machine-local operational
# state, not a record — it names an absolute `source` path and stamps the market vintage of the
# machine that captured. Tracking it meant the `COPY . .` image carried ONE machine's stamp into
# EVERY container, so a fresh box container arrived pre-seeded with a laptop capture pointing at a
# /Users/... path and a different board. The guard REFUSED it (which is why this is a finding and
# not an incident) — but a stamp that ships in the image is a trap waiting for the next reader who
# does not validate it. The audit trail is NOT lost: the run's report embeds the stamp verbatim
# under `capture`, and the report IS tracked.
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/artifacts/nf_inj2b_baseline/nf_inj2c_capture.json
.nf_c8_red_proof_backup/
# NF-W7h's RED proof mutates REAL source and runs INSIDE the collected pytest suite, so a killed
# run can leave both the mutation and its on-disk backup behind. The mutation is repaired at the
# next import; the backup must never be committable (2026-09-03: a sweeping commit shipped the
# mutations themselves to `dev`, deleting a §0.5 gate clause on a decided story).
*.nf_w7h_red_proof_backup
.nf_w7h_red_proof.lock

# NF-INJ3b-M (PM ruling D4): the neutral "latest run" stems that
# run_nf_tr2b_placement_read / run_interval_revalidation now write BY DEFAULT, so a session
# running them as a gate cannot clobber a DECIDED story's record. They are scratch: the decided
# artifacts are the tracked ones, refreshed only by an explicit `--out <decided stem>`.
# ⛔ Do NOT ignore the decided stems themselves.
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/ablation_results/*_latest.json
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/ablation_results/*_latest.md
# NF-INJ2c node 4: a `--folds` SMOKE writes its own stem so a code-path proof can never clobber the
# decided artifact (NF-INJ3b-M D4). The smoke output is scratch and is not a record.
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/ablation_results/nf_inj2c_decisive_smoke.json
quant_sports_intel_models/football/nfl/fantasy/ablation_results/nf_inj2c_decisive_smoke.md
